I think that the ingress class defaulting happen in the admission plugin

https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/388c2d901d185d34a340fcae566bd38b73bdb704/plugin/pkg/admission/network/defaultingressclass/admission.go#L82-L84

@robscott @rikatz you are more familiar than me with this, is it possible that the update is not being handled by the admission plugin?

Do we want to allow changing the ingress class after creation?  Or should we patch that up on an update to nil?

Or is this a case of 2 clients fighting over the object ownership, and "don't do that"?

@bowei @robscott

> So I think the "safest" answer is to recognize that changing ingressClassName from any value to nil is almost certainly an error and just patch it up with the previous value. I do not think we should automatically change nil -> default at all. The open question is whether to allow changing nil -> value or value-A -> value-B after creation? It seems semantically correct but likely to be buggy.

I'm not as familiar with the use cases, but is not possible to hot loop if someone is trying to delete it? 

```
...loop {
  if ingress.ingressClassName != "" {
     delete(ingress.ingressClassName)
  }
}
```
